@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Liberty personal accident insurance rules, UW-PAG-W-001-10-V
-- (Quy tắc bảo hiểm tai nạn con người, Công ty TNHH Bảo hiểm Liberty).
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every other module imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../source/raw/liberty-pa.txt, the `pdftotext -layout` rendering of the insurer's
-- PDF (PDF sha256 d6b89ba1...5ee9; text sha256 b0711cb9...55ad), retrieved 2026-10-06.
-- `src N` in a comment points at line N of that file. Vietnamese is quoted only on
-- `-- src:N |` lines generated by tools/vnsrc.py, and in short runs that the same tool checks
-- occur verbatim in the source.
--
-- Money is Vietnamese đồng (VND), a bare NUMBER. A rate is a fraction: 40% is 0.4.
-- Dates are calendar dates. How each period is counted (days, weeks, months) is said where the
-- rule counts it, and every choice is a fork in NOTES.md section 3.
--
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the
-- fact, or the policy schedule, a medical report or the claim file records it. Whether the
-- fact makes a benefit payable is a rule, and belongs in the module that says so.
--
-- WHAT THE DOCUMENT LEAVES TO THE SCHEDULE. The wording repeatedly hands figures to the
-- policy summary (Bản tóm tắt Hợp đồng bảo hiểm) or the certificate (Giấy chứng nhận bảo
-- hiểm): the period, each benefit's limit, the temporary-injury basis and day limits, the daily
-- hospital allowance, the geographical area. Each is an input below with no default.

§ `Nouns`

§§ `The insured and their place in the group`

-- The policyholder is an organisation (src 34) insuring a group (src 188-195): the employees
-- of an employer, or the members of a sponsoring organisation, with their dependants.
-- A dependant (src 104-114) is a spouse, a partner living as spouse, or an unmarried child the
-- insured member must support. The kinds of child the definition lists (natural, born outside
-- marriage, stepchild, lawfully adopted) are not told apart by any rule.
DECLARE `A dependant's relationship to the insured member` IS ONE OF
    `a spouse lawfully married to the insured member`
    `a person living with the insured member as husband or wife`
    `an unmarried child the insured member has a duty to support`

DECLARE `A place in the group` IS ONE OF
    `an employee of the employer`                         -- src 179-181
    `a member of the sponsoring organisation`             -- src 174-177, 197-199
    `a dependant` HAS `the relationship` IS A `A dependant's relationship to the insured member`

-- Occupation classes 1 to 4 (src 280-304). Which class an occupation falls in is decided
-- against the class descriptions, of which the listed jobs are only examples; it is an input.
DECLARE `An occupation class` IS ONE OF
    `class 1`
    `class 2`
    `class 3`
    `class 4`

DECLARE `A side of the body` IS ONE OF
    `the right side`
    `the left side`

-- The insured person, as the application, the schedule and their documents record them.
-- * `living in Vietnam when cover began, as declared in the application`, and
--   `living in Vietnam on a tourist visa`: the facts the definition of the country of
--   residence turns on (src 130-135).
-- * `left-handed`: MAYBE, because it matters only for an arm or hand injury (src 413-414); an
--   arm or hand claim with NOTHING here is refused by name, not guessed.
-- * `degree of permanent disability before the effective date`: a fraction (0.5 is 50%),
--   general exclusion 6(j) (src 797).
-- * `insured under the same contract as a parent, adoptive parent or legal guardian`: the
--   condition for insuring a minor (src 1167-1169).
-- * `in full-time study, with a valid student card or proof of it`: dependants aged over 18
--   and not over 23 (src 108-114).
-- * `keeps a valid visa or temporary residence card`: foreigners resident in Vietnam
--   (src 1170-1178).
DECLARE `An insured person` HAS
    `date of birth`                                                         IS A DATE
    `place in the group`                                                    IS A `A place in the group`
    `a Vietnamese citizen`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `living in Vietnam when cover began, as declared in the application`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `living in Vietnam on a tourist visa`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a citizen of a country under United Nations, United States, European Union or United Kingdom sanctions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `occupation class`                                                      IS AN `An occupation class`
    `left-handed`                                                           IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `degree of permanent disability before the effective date`              IS A NUMBER
    `insured under the same contract as a parent, adoptive parent or legal guardian` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in full-time study, with a valid student card or proof of it`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `keeps a valid visa or temporary residence card`                        IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The policy schedule`

-- Benefit B is paid on one of two bases the schedule chooses (src 479-484).
DECLARE `The temporary injury basis` IS ONE OF
    `a fixed sum for each day` HAS `the daily sum` IS A NUMBER
    `the insured's monthly income`

DECLARE `The temporary injury benefit chosen` HAS
    `basis`                         IS A `The temporary injury basis`
    `limit`                         IS A NUMBER
    `maximum days for each injury`  IS A NUMBER
    `maximum days in the period`    IS A NUMBER

-- The policy summary or certificate for one insured (src 54-56, 73-75). A benefit the
-- policyholder did not choose (src 311-314) is NOTHING: the source contemplates its absence.
-- * `death limit` and `permanent injury limit`: benefit A (src 324-342). The wording speaks of
--   one limit for "Tử vong hay Thương tật vĩnh viễn" but limitation 1(b)-(c) compares a
--   death limit with a permanent injury limit, so the two are carried separately.
-- * `medical expense limit`: benefit C (src 509-511), an aggregate for the period.
-- * `daily hospital allowance`: benefit D (src 518-521), per 24 hours.
-- * `food poisoning cover agreed`: special provision 9 (src 656-660).
DECLARE `The policy schedule` HAS
    `first day of the period of insurance`  IS A DATE
    `last day of the period of insurance`   IS A DATE
    `a renewal`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `worldwide geographical scope`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `death limit`                           IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `permanent injury limit`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `temporary injury benefit`              IS A MAYBE `The temporary injury benefit chosen`
    `medical expense limit`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `daily hospital allowance`              IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `food poisoning cover agreed`           IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The accident`

-- A condition of the insured's health that existed before cover, described by the three
-- facts the definition of a pre-existing condition turns on (src 246-259).
DECLARE `A prior condition` HAS
    `existed before the effective date, with signs or symptoms the insured knew or should have known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `treatment, medicine, advice or diagnosis sought or received before the contract began`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insured knew it existed before the contract began`                                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- Everything that was part of, or a cause of, the accident and that some provision of the
-- wording names. One constructor per limb named; where the limb carries its own exception,
-- the exception is a field. A circumstance no provision names is simply not listed.
-- The list is the record of WHAT HAPPENED: whether it excludes or extends cover is the rule
-- in lpa-exclusions.l4 or lpa-special-provisions.l4.
DECLARE `A circumstance of the accident` IS ONE OF
    -- general exclusion 1 (src 668-674)
    `nuclear weapons material`
    `ionising radiation or radioactive contamination from nuclear fuel or nuclear waste`
    `the radioactive, explosive or other hazardous properties of a nuclear explosive assembly`
    -- general exclusion 2 (src 676-696); special exclusion 1 (src 883)
    `war, invasion, act of a foreign enemy, hostilities or civil war`
    `rebellion, civil commotion, mutiny, insurrection, revolution, military or usurped power, martial law or state of siege`
    `an act of terrorism`
    `action taken to control, prevent or suppress war, rebellion or terrorism`
    -- general exclusion 3 (src 707-717)
    `travel by air` HAS `as a passenger in an aircraft fully licensed to carry passengers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `aircrew, commercial, technical or sporting activity relating to aircraft`
    `vehicle racing, as driver or passenger`
    `test driving, or a test-driving programme or event`
    -- general exclusion 4, taking part in or training for (src 719-745)
    `hunting`
    `being airborne`
    `parachuting`
    `gliding, paragliding, display parachuting, parasailing, hang gliding or flying` HAS `as a ticketed passenger on a licensed commercial aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a race, or a test of speed or endurance`
    `mountaineering, rock climbing, long-distance walking, backpacking or hitch-hiking`
    `scuba diving, underwater breathing apparatus, wrestling, boxing, acrobatics or a similar sport`
    `horse racing, equestrian competition or polo`
    `winter sports or ice hockey`
    `surfing or sailing` HAS `distance from shore in kilometres` IS A NUMBER
    `a professional sport, or any sport as a professional`
    `training for or taking part in a sports competition, or racing other than on foot`
    `caving, bungee jumping, martial arts, ballooning, a sponsored organised sport, or another adventurous activity`
    -- general exclusion 5 (src 747-772)
    `intentional self-injury or suicide, sane or insane`
    `fighting or deliberately putting oneself in danger` HAS `to save a life, or confirmed by the authorities as self-defence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a pre-existing physical or mental defect or infirmity`
    `being under the influence of drugs, addictive substances or medicine` HAS `medicine prescribed by a Doctor, not for drug addiction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intoxication, drugs, alcohol, stimulants, or insanity from natural causes` HAS `the insured knew beforehand that the condition was present` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a condition of the insured` HAS `the condition` IS A `A prior condition`
    `a complication of surgery, or an accident in the course of surgery, of treatment of illness, or of maternity`
    `poisoning by food or drink` HAS `beyond the insured's control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `inhaling smoke, toxic vapour, gas or poison` HAS `sudden, causing asphyxiation`                        IS A BOOLEAN
                                                      `from a premeditated and deliberate act of the insured` IS A BOOLEAN
    `kidnap for ransom or hostage-taking`
    -- general exclusion 6 (src 774-799)
    `a breach of the law, of local regulations, or of the rules of a lawfully established body, intentional or not`
    `working on a ship, boat or other waterway vehicle`
    `service in the navy, army, air force or a professional fire service`
    `military training exercises, or combat by the armed forces`
    `serving as a member of the armed forces or police`
    `performing work`
    `testing any conveyance`
    `offshore activity, aerial photography, handling explosives, or an occupation dangerous by height, depth or heat` HAS `with the Company's written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `working at a height` HAS `height in metres`                 IS A NUMBER
                              `with the Company's written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `using a timber saw or band saw`
    `a nervous or mental illness or disorder that leaves the insured unable to understand or control their behaviour`
    `leprosy`
    `work connected with mines`
    -- general exclusions 7, 8, 15, 18, 20 (src 802-816, 859-876)
    `asbestos`
    `DES, dioxin, urea formaldehyde, SARS, avian influenza or TSE`
    `AIDS, an AIDS-related complex or a similar syndrome`
    `a deliberate act of the insured, a beneficiary or a lawful heir to cause harm`
    `a disease declared or assessed a pandemic by the WHO or another competent authority`
    `a circumstance the schedule or certificate excludes`
    -- special exclusions 4 to 6 (src 891-1061)
    `nuclear reaction, nuclear radiation or radioactive contamination`
    `property at a nuclear installation, nuclear fuel or material, or supplying such an installation`
    -- special exclusion 9 (src 1105-1112)
    `paying the claim would breach a United Nations, European Union, United Kingdom or United States sanction`
    -- special provisions 2 to 5 and 8 (src 594-653)
    `unavoidable exposure to the weather or the elements, after an injury`
    `murder or assault on the insured` HAS `the insured was complicit in it or provoked it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hijacking of a conveyance` HAS `the insured was a ticketed passenger on a conveyance licensed to carry passengers` IS A BOOLEAN
                                    `the insured took part in it or provoked it`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `riding a motorcycle, as driver or passenger` HAS `engine capacity in cc` IS A NUMBER

-- The accident and the injury, as a claim file records them.
-- The five limbs of the definition of an Accident (src 145-149) and the negative limb of the
-- definition of an Injury (src 151-154) are facts a medical report or an accident report
-- states; whether they add up to an Accident is the rule in lpa-definitions.l4.
DECLARE `An accident` HAS
    `date of the accident`                                                 IS A DATE
    `sudden`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by an external and visible force on the insured's body`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused harm to the insured's body`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `unintended by the insured and beyond the insured's control`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the direct and sole cause of the injury or death`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury came from illness, gradual mental or physical wear, deterioration of health, age, disability or degeneration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within the geographical area in the schedule`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `circumstances`                                                        IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of the accident`

-- Special provision 1 (src 586-592): a disappearance with a conveyance.
DECLARE `A disappearance` HAS
    `date of the disappearance`                                            IS A DATE
    `the conveyance the insured travelled on sank, was wrecked or crashed`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `in circumstances the contract covers`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `date the body was found`                                              IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `Permanent injuries`

DECLARE `A finger` IS ONE OF
    `the thumb`
    `the index finger`
    `the middle finger`
    `the ring finger`
    `the little finger`

DECLARE `A toe` IS ONE OF
    `the big toe`
    `the second toe`
    `the third toe`
    `the fourth toe`
    `the little toe`

-- One constructor per printed row of the two tables of benefit A.2 (src 344-450), in the
-- order printed. The rates are in lpa-injury-tables.l4. A row includes the total loss of
-- function of the limb or part it names, which the wording treats as its loss (src 461-462).
DECLARE `A part of the tables` IS ONE OF
    `total permanent injury`              -- THƯƠNG TẬT TOÀN BỘ VĨNH VIỄN
    `partial permanent injury, the head`  -- ĐẦU
    `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`

DECLARE `A row of the permanent injury tables` IS ONE OF
    `total and incurable blindness of both eyes`                                   -- src 346
    `total and incurable mental disorder`                                          -- src 348
    `loss of both arms or both hands`                                              -- src 350
    `total deafness of both ears`                                                  -- src 351
    `removal of the lower jaw`                                                     -- src 352
    `loss of speech`                                                               -- src 353
    `loss of one arm and one foot, one arm and one leg, one hand and one leg, or one hand and one foot` -- src 354
    `loss of both legs or both feet`                                               -- src 357
    `loss of part of the skull, through its full thickness, over more than 6 cm2`  -- src 364
    `loss of part of the skull, through its full thickness, over 3 cm2 to 6 cm2`   -- src 365
    `removal of part of the lower jaw, of a whole branch of the upper jaw, or of half the upper jaw` -- src 366
    `loss of one eye`                                                              -- src 368
    `total deafness of one ear`                                                    -- src 369
    `loss of more than 8 teeth that cannot be replaced by dentures`                -- src 371
    `loss of 5 to 7 teeth`                                                         -- src 372
    `loss of 3 to 4 teeth`                                                         -- src 373
    `loss of 1 to 3 teeth`                                                         -- src 374
    `loss of an arm or a hand`                                                     -- src 381
    `loss of the main part of the bone of the upper arm`                           -- src 382
    `complete paralysis of the upper arm`                                          -- src 385
    `complete paralysis of the circumflex nerve`                                   -- src 387
    `ankylosis of the shoulder`                                                    -- src 388
    `ankylosis of the elbow in a favourable position`                              -- src 390
    `ankylosis of the elbow in an unfavourable position`                           -- src 391
    `loss of the main part of both bones of the forearm`                           -- src 392
    `complete paralysis of the median nerve`                                       -- src 395
    `complete paralysis of the radial nerve in the arm`                            -- src 396
    `complete paralysis of the radial nerve in the hand`                           -- src 397
    `complete paralysis of the ulnar nerve`                                        -- src 398
    `ankylosis of the wrist in a favourable position`                              -- src 399
    `ankylosis of the wrist in an unfavourable position`                           -- src 401
    `amputation of the whole thumb`                                                -- src 403
    `amputation of the whole index finger`                                         -- src 404
    `amputation of the thumb and the index finger together`                        -- src 405
    `amputation of the thumb and one finger other than the index finger`           -- src 406
    `amputation of 3 fingers including the thumb`                                  -- src 407
    `amputation of 3 fingers other than the thumb and the index finger`            -- src 408
    `amputation of 4 fingers including the thumb`                                  -- src 409
    `amputation of 4 fingers other than the thumb`                                 -- src 410
    `amputation of one finger other than the thumb and the index finger`           -- src 411
    `amputation of a thigh, upper half`                                            -- src 418
    `amputation of a thigh, lower half`                                            -- src 420
    `total loss of a foot, by tibio-tarsal disarticulation`                        -- src 422
    `partial loss of a foot, by sub-talar disarticulation`                         -- src 424
    `partial loss of a foot, by medio-tarsal disarticulation`                      -- src 426
    `partial loss of a foot, by tarso-metatarsal disarticulation`                  -- src 427
    `complete paralysis of a lower leg`                                            -- src 428
    `complete paralysis of the external popliteal nerve`                           -- src 430
    `complete paralysis of the internal popliteal nerve`                           -- src 431
    `complete paralysis of both the internal and external popliteal nerves`        -- src 435
    `ankylosis of the hip`                                                         -- src 437
    `ankylosis of the knee`                                                        -- src 438
    `loss of most of the femur or of most of both bones of the lower leg`          -- src 439
    `loss of most of the kneecap, in many fragments, hindering movement between lower leg and thigh` -- src 441
    `loss of most of the kneecap, movement still possible`                         -- src 443
    `shortening of a leg by at least about 5 cm`                                   -- src 445
    `shortening of a leg by 3 to 5 cm`                                             -- src 447
    `amputation of 4 toes including the big toe`                                   -- src 448
    `amputation of 3 toes including the big toe`                                   -- src 449
    `amputation of the big toe`                                                    -- src 450

-- How a printed rate reads: one column, or a column for each side (src 379).
DECLARE `The printed rate` IS ONE OF
    `one rate` HAS `the rate` IS A NUMBER
    `a rate for each side` HAS `on the right` IS A NUMBER
                               `on the left`  IS A NUMBER

-- A permanent injury as a medical assessment describes it. Rows the assessor can name go in
-- `an injury in a row of the tables`; the rest are described by the facts the tables
-- measure (fingers, toes, teeth, area of skull, centimetres of shortening), and the rules in
-- lpa-injury-tables.l4 find the row, or find that there is none.
-- `an injury not in the tables` carries the rate the Company decided, by comparison with the
-- tables (src 459-465): NOTHING until the Company has decided.
DECLARE `A permanent injury` IS ONE OF
    `an injury in a row of the tables` HAS `the row`  IS A `A row of the permanent injury tables`
                                           `the side` IS A `A side of the body`
    `loss of the remaining eye, the other having been lost before the accident`
    `amputation of fingers of one hand` HAS `the fingers` IS A LIST OF `A finger`
                                            `the side`    IS A `A side of the body`
    `amputation of toes of one foot` HAS `the toes` IS A LIST OF `A toe`
    `ankylosis of the joints of fingers of one hand` HAS `the fingers` IS A LIST OF `A finger`
                                                         `the side`    IS A `A side of the body`
    `ankylosis of the joints of toes of one foot` HAS `the toes` IS A LIST OF `A toe`
    `loss of teeth` HAS `the number of teeth`           IS A NUMBER
                        `can be replaced by dentures`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `loss of part of the skull through its full thickness` HAS `the area in square centimetres` IS A NUMBER
    `shortening of a leg` HAS `the shortening in centimetres` IS A NUMBER
    `an injury not in the tables` HAS `the rate the Company decided` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- Limitation 1(a) (src 548-550): whether, for the same injury, an item falls within another
-- claimed item with a larger amount is the assessor's finding, so it is an input per item.
DECLARE `A claimed permanent injury` HAS
    `the injury`                                                             IS A `A permanent injury`
    `within another claimed item with a larger amount, for the same injury`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- The assessment that permanence turns on (src 156-163): the injury lasted continuously from
-- the accident, and at the end of the period there was no hope of recovery.
DECLARE `The permanent injury claim` HAS
    `date of the assessment`                                                 IS A DATE
    `the injury lasted continuously from the accident to the assessment`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `no hope of recovery at the assessment`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `items`                                                                  IS A LIST OF `A claimed permanent injury`

§§ `Temporary injury, medical expenses and hospital days`

-- Benefit B (src 469-507). `monthly income at the time of the accident` is the Income of
-- src 242-244 or the insured's latest declaration confirmed by the Company (src 490-499);
-- NOTHING where neither is in the file.
DECLARE `The temporary injury claim` HAS
    `first day of total disablement`                                    IS A DATE
    `last day of total disablement`                                     IS A DATE
    `still receiving income, wages or business income`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `monthly income at the time of the accident`                        IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `date death or permanent injury was determined for payment`         IS A MAYBE DATE
    `days already paid in the period for other injuries`                IS A NUMBER
    `amount already paid under benefit B in the period`                 IS A NUMBER
    `also insured under another contract, other than social insurance`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- What a medical bill was for, at the grain the wording distinguishes (src 229-240, 509-516,
-- 818-866, 885).
DECLARE `A kind of medical expense` IS ONE OF
    `a hospital stay or outpatient treatment`
    `a general practitioner, a specialist, traditional medicine or bone-setting`
    `dental surgery`
    `surgery`
    `x-rays`
    `medical services`
    `medicine and medical supplies`
    `nursing home care or nursing`
    `dental scaling, polishing, extraction, x-ray, implant, root canal, tumour or root-tip removal, cosmetic treatment, crown, bridge, denture or filling`
    `other dental treatment`
    `dietary supplements or natural substances bought without prescription`
    `a prosthesis, orthosis, replacement device, rehabilitation or medical equipment, mobility aid, hearing or sight aid, wheelchair, crutch or other device`
    `cosmetic treatment, cosmetic surgery, plastic surgery or reconstruction after an accident`
    `experimental or scientifically unproven treatment`
    `treatment relating to maternity, pregnancy, miscarriage or abortion`

-- One bill. `the reasonable and customary amount` is the market figure of src 261-266: a
-- judgement about what comparable facilities charge, so an input.
DECLARE `A medical expense` HAS
    `kind`                                                      IS A `A kind of medical expense`
    `amount paid by the insured`                                IS A NUMBER
    `the reasonable and customary amount`                       IS A NUMBER
    `date incurred`                                             IS A DATE
    `to treat the injury from the accident`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `directed by a Doctor`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `for professional services of a Doctor at a Medical Facility` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a pandemic declaration in force on the date incurred`      IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `The medical expense claim` HAS
    `expenses`                                                  IS A LIST OF `A medical expense`
    `also insured under another contract, other than social insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount met by another contract or another source`          IS A NUMBER
    `amount already paid under benefit C in the period`         IS A NUMBER

-- Benefit D (src 223-227, 518-521).
DECLARE `The hospital allowance claim` HAS
    `date of admission`                                         IS A DATE
    `hospital treatment was required for the injury`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours of treatment in a Medical Facility`                  IS A NUMBER
    `also insured under another contract, other than social insurance` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Cover in force`

-- General provision 7 (src 1245-1342) ends one insured's cover on the earliest of several
-- dates. These records carry the facts behind each date.
DECLARE `An absence from Vietnam` HAS
    `date of leaving Vietnam`                    IS A DATE
    `consecutive days outside Vietnam`           IS A NUMBER
    `notified the Company beforehand`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Company agreed to continue cover`       IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `A change increasing the risk` HAS
    `date of the change`                         IS A DATE
    `notified to the Company immediately`        IS A BOOLEAN

-- * `date of entry into Vietnam`, `date the insured became eligible`: the deferred start of the
--   period of insurance (src 77-83), NOTHING where it does not apply.
-- * the other MAYBE dates are the events of 7.1-7.3, NOTHING where the event has not happened.
-- * `premium for the insured paid in full within the payment period`: 7.1(d), 7.2(d), 7.3(d).
DECLARE `The insured's cover facts` HAS
    `date of entry into Vietnam, if after the first day of the period`      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the insured became eligible, if after the first day of the period` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the insured ceased to be eligible, for a reason other than age`   IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the group contract ended`                                         IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date employment with the employer ended`                               IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date membership of the sponsoring organisation ended`                  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the insured member's own cover ended`                             IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the benefits were used up`                                        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `premium for the insured paid in full within the payment period`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `last day of the payment period`                                        IS A DATE
    `absences from Vietnam`                                                 IS A LIST OF `An absence from Vietnam`
    `changes increasing the risk`                                           IS A LIST OF `A change increasing the risk`

§§ `The claim`

DECLARE `A claim document` IS ONE OF
    `the claim form, completed on the Company's form, signed by the claimant and signed and stamped by the policyholder`
    `the accident report`
    `the injury certificate`
    `the death certificate`
    `the certificate of lawful inheritance`
    `the treating Doctor's direction to rest, or the social insurance sick-leave certificate`
    `the medical treatment records`
    `the timesheet and the labour contract or agreement`

-- General provision 13 (src 1476-1516).
DECLARE `The claim procedure` HAS
    `date written notice of the injury was given`                    IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the claim forms and supporting evidence were returned`     IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the claim file was submitted`                              IS A MAYBE DATE
    `documents supplied`                                             IS A LIST OF `A claim document`
    `originals supplied, or copies the Company accepted`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insured used the services the treating Doctor directed and had the treatment the Doctor considered medically necessary` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Facts about the contract and the claim that the conditions precedent, fraud, change of
-- risk and beneficiary provisions turn on (src 1142-1243).
DECLARE `The claim facts` HAS
    `all statements and declarations in the application complete, true and accurate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is false or fraudulent`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim arises from a change the Company was not told of, or did not agree to cover` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a beneficiary was designated`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Outcomes`

-- Who receives a payment (src 24-26, 591-592, 1184-1188, 1505-1506).
DECLARE `A payee` IS ONE OF
    `the insured`
    `the policyholder, authorised by the insured`
    `the beneficiary designated`
    `the insured's lawful heirs or legal representative`

-- Every exclusion the wording prints, one constructor per limb, numbered as printed.
-- `general exclusion` is ĐIỀU KHOẢN LOẠI TRỪ CHUNG (src 664-876); `special exclusion` is
-- NHỮNG LOẠI TRỪ ĐẶC BIỆT (src 881-1112).
DECLARE `An exclusion` IS ONE OF
    `general exclusion 1(a), nuclear weapons material`
    `general exclusion 1(b), ionising radiation or contamination from nuclear fuel or waste`
    `general exclusion 1(c), a nuclear explosive assembly`
    `general exclusion 2(a), war`
    `general exclusion 2(b), rebellion, revolution or martial law`
    `general exclusion 2(c), terrorism`
    `general exclusion 2, action to control, prevent or suppress 2(a) to 2(c)`
    `general exclusion 3(a), air travel other than as a passenger in a licensed passenger aircraft`
    `general exclusion 3(b), aircrew, commercial, technical or sporting activity relating to aircraft`
    `general exclusion 3(c), vehicle racing`
    `general exclusion 3(d), test driving`
    `general exclusion 4(a), hunting`
    `general exclusion 4(b), being airborne`
    `general exclusion 4(c), parachuting`
    `general exclusion 4(d), gliding or flying other than as a ticketed passenger`
    `general exclusion 4(e), a race or a speed or endurance test`
    `general exclusion 4(f), mountaineering, rock climbing, long-distance walking`
    `general exclusion 4(g), diving, wrestling, boxing, acrobatics`
    `general exclusion 4(h), horse racing, equestrian sport, polo`
    `general exclusion 4(i), winter sports, ice hockey`
    `general exclusion 4(j), surfing or sailing 5 km from shore`
    `general exclusion 4(k), professional sport`
    `general exclusion 4(l), sports competition or racing other than on foot`
    `general exclusion 4(m), caving, bungee, martial arts, ballooning, adventurous activity`
    `general exclusion 5(a), self-injury, suicide, fighting or deliberate danger`
    `general exclusion 5(b), a pre-existing defect or infirmity`
    `general exclusion 5(c), drugs, addictive substances or unprescribed medicine`
    `general exclusion 5(d), intoxication or insanity known beforehand`
    `general exclusion 5(e), a pre-existing condition`
    `general exclusion 5(f), complications of surgery, treatment or maternity`
    `general exclusion 5(g), food or drink poisoning, or inhaling toxic vapour, gas or poison`
    `general exclusion 5(h), kidnap for ransom`
    `general exclusion 6(a), a breach of the law or regulations`
    `general exclusion 6(b), working on a vessel`
    `general exclusion 6(c), naval, military, air force or professional fire service`
    `general exclusion 6(d), military exercises, combat, armed forces or police`
    `general exclusion 6(e), testing a conveyance`
    `general exclusion 6(f), offshore or height, depth or heat work, or above 30 metres`
    `general exclusion 6(g), timber saws or band saws`
    `general exclusion 6(h), nervous or mental illness`
    `general exclusion 6(i), leprosy`
    `general exclusion 6(j), permanent disability of 50% or more before the effective date`
    `general exclusion 6(k), work connected with mines`
    `general exclusion 7, asbestos`
    `general exclusion 8(a), DES, dioxin, urea formaldehyde, SARS, avian influenza, TSE`
    `general exclusion 8(b), AIDS`
    `general exclusion 15, a deliberate act of the insured, a beneficiary or an heir`
    `general exclusion 18, a pandemic disease`
    `general exclusion 19, occupation class 4`
    `general exclusion 20, an exclusion in the schedule or certificate`
    `special exclusion 1, war risks`
    `special exclusion 5, nuclear reaction, radiation or contamination`
    `special exclusion 9, sanctions`

-- One side of the contract or the other: who bears a burden of proof (general exclusion 2,
-- src 697-700) or a cost (general provision 12, src 1472-1474).
DECLARE `A side to the contract` IS ONE OF
    `the policyholder or the insured`
    `the Company`

-- Why no benefit is payable on a claim. A list of these is the answer to "is the event
-- covered?": an empty list means covered.
DECLARE `A reason no benefit is payable` IS ONE OF
    `not an Accident as the wording defines it`
    `not an Injury as the wording defines it`
    `the accident was not within the period of insurance`
    `the insured's cover was not in force on the date of the accident`
    `the injury did not occur within the geographical area`
    `the insured is not eligible to be insured`
    `excluded by` HAS `the exclusion` IS AN `An exclusion`
    `special provision 3: the insured was complicit in or provoked the murder or assault`
    `special provision 4: the insured was not a ticketed passenger, or took part in or provoked the hijacking`
    `special provision 8: the motorcycle was over 150cc`
    `special provision 1: the conveyance did not sink, wreck or crash, or the circumstances are not covered`
    `condition precedent 4(a)(i): the declarations were not complete, true and accurate`
    `condition precedent 4(a)(ii): the premium was not paid in full within the payment period`
    `general provision 5: the claim is false or fraudulent`
    `general provision 6: the claim arises from a change the Company was not told of or did not accept`
    `general provision 13(d): the claim was not made within the time or by the procedure`

§§ `The contract, the parties' acts, and the claim as a whole`

-- The documents that make up the contract, in general provision 1's order (src 1121-1130).
DECLARE `A contract document` IS ONE OF
    `the application, quotation, renewal notice or renewal quotation`
    `an endorsement`
    `the certificate or the summary`
    `the insurance programme`
    `these rules`

-- What the Company may do on a failure to disclose (general provision 2(a), src 1149-1153).
DECLARE `A remedy for non-disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `reduce the benefit`
    `refuse the claim`
    `cancel the contract from the effective date`

-- The actors and acts of the regulative rules (general provisions 13, 14, 16).
DECLARE `An actor` IS ONE OF
    `the insured`
    `the policyholder`
    `the Company`
    `a party to the dispute`

DECLARE `An act` IS ONE OF
    `give written notice of the injury`
    `return the claim forms with supporting evidence`
    `submit the claim file`
    `pay the premium due`
    `bring the dispute before a Vietnamese court`

-- The five benefits (src 320-521).
DECLARE `A benefit` IS ONE OF
    `benefit A.1, death`
    `benefit A.2, permanent injury`
    `benefit B, temporary injury`
    `benefit C, medical expenses`
    `benefit D, hospital allowance`

-- The grounds on which one insured's cover ends (general provision 7, src 1245-1342).
DECLARE `A ground for the end of cover` IS ONE OF
    `the insured ceased to be eligible`
    `the group contract ended`
    `employment with the employer ended`
    `membership of the sponsoring organisation ended`
    `the insured member's own cover ended`
    `the premium was not paid in full within the payment period`
    `the insured left Vietnam for over 180 consecutive days without notice or agreement`
    `a change increasing the risk was not notified immediately`
    `the benefits were used up`
    `the period of insurance ended`

-- One claim, whole: the insured, the schedule, the facts of cover, the accident, the claim
-- facts and procedure, and what happened after the accident. A benefit not claimed is NOTHING.
DECLARE `A claim` HAS
    `the insured`                          IS AN `An insured person`
    `the schedule`                         IS A `The policy schedule`
    `the cover facts`                      IS A `The insured's cover facts`
    `the accident`                         IS AN `An accident`
    `the facts`                            IS A `The claim facts`
    `the procedure`                        IS A `The claim procedure`
    `date of death`                        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `permanent injury`                     IS A MAYBE `The permanent injury claim`
    `temporary injury`                     IS A MAYBE `The temporary injury claim`
    `medical expenses`                     IS A MAYBE `The medical expense claim`
    `hospital allowance`                   IS A MAYBE `The hospital allowance claim`

-- The answer to a claim: why it is not covered (empty if covered), the benefits that fail for
-- want of time or procedure, and what each benefit pays.
DECLARE `The decision on a claim` HAS
    `reasons no benefit is payable`        IS A LIST OF `A reason no benefit is payable`
    `benefits void under general provision 13(d)` IS A LIST OF `A benefit`
    `death benefit`                        IS A NUMBER
    `permanent injury benefit`             IS A NUMBER
    `temporary injury benefit`             IS A NUMBER
    `medical expense benefit`              IS A NUMBER
    `hospital allowance`                   IS A NUMBER
    `total payable`                        IS A NUMBER
